From 2677746cc1d6b6ab4aa60dbb5c8ad926fb327568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:05:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/qcom-mpm: Unregister the provider on probe failure

The MPM driver publishes its genpd provider before requesting the mailbox,
finding the parent IRQ domain, creating its IRQ domain and requesting the
interrupt. A mailbox error returns without removing either the provider or
the initialized domain. Later failures remove the domain but leave its OF
provider registered. Probe can fail with EPROBE_DEFER here, leaving a stale
provider referring to device-managed memory released after the failure.

Unregister the OF provider before removing the initialized genpd on every
failure after provider registration. Route mailbox acquisition failures
through that cleanup without attempting to free an unacquired mailbox.
The existing domain and mailbox cleanup remains in place for later errors.

A host model executes the actual probe and mapping helper with synthetic
DT, devres, genpd, mailbox and IRQ services. Its 64 cases reproduce 28
cleanup assertion failures before this change and pass afterward, covering
ordinary and local sleep-coordinator configurations, deferred/hard errors
at all checked initialization boundaries, and invalid pin counts. Four
clean controls reject missing or reordered cleanup. Native ARM/ARM64 normal
and RT object builds pass with no new diagnostics. Real kernel concurrency
and hardware probing remain unqualified.

Codex found the issue and generated this fix, host model and draft message
during the Fx0 power-controller audit. Public source history verifies that
the original MPM driver registered the provider without these error-path
releases. Human review and DCO remain pending. Nothing has been submitted.

Fixes: a6199bb514d8 ("irqchip: Add Qualcomm MPM controller driver")

Backport to the maintained 6.18.63 Fx0 integration. Original integration
model evidence remains separate. In the combined three-fix series, the
relevant focused model passes 43 cases. The complete series also compiles
on ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT with nonpermissive CFI. ARM32 RT is unsupported
in this maintained kernel and is not counted as an RT build.

Codex prepared this local backport and its verification. Human review
and DCO remain pending; the MPM issue also awaits human security
classification. Nothing has been published or sent to maintainers.

Backported from commit a80e0ad0e69ac36427d90305dc592298f7132b03
("irqchip/qcom-mpm: Unregister the provider on probe failure").
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
index 181320528a47..c6aaba6c5c1c 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
@@ -441,7 +441,7 @@ static int qcom_mpm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev, struct device_node *pare
 	if (IS_ERR(priv->mbox_chan)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(priv->mbox_chan);
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to acquire IPC channel: %d\n", ret);
-		return ret;
+		goto remove_provider;
 	}
 
 	parent_domain = irq_find_host(parent);
@@ -475,6 +475,8 @@ static int qcom_mpm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev, struct device_node *pare
 	irq_domain_remove(priv->domain);
 free_mbox:
 	mbox_free_channel(priv->mbox_chan);
+remove_provider:
+	of_genpd_del_provider(np);
 remove_genpd:
 	pm_genpd_remove(genpd);
 	return ret;
-- 
